{"op":"setSummary","target":"jira:SYN-45","ref":null,"args":{"summary":"Rebooking: keep the original fare on long crossings when moving to a dearer sailing"}}
They replace the 1 change an earlier run in this turn captured, and become the change set the user reviews when this turn ends.
Once applied, the user undoes them with Revert in the thread, which proposes the reverse as a new change set.
Nothing is sent until the user approves: say you proposed them, never that they're done.

